From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Use build.verbose instead of the removed cmake.verbose

scikit-build-core renamed `cmake.verbose` to `build.verbose` in 0.10 and
kept the old key as a deprecation warning through 0.12.x. Starting with
1.0, an unset `minimum-version` turns that warning into a hard error in
get_requires_for_build_wheel:

  ERROR: Use build.verbose instead of cmake.verbose for scikit-build-core >= 0.10

`[build-system] requires` leaves scikit-build-core unpinned, so any fresh
build of this tag now resolves 1.x and fails before CMake runs, on every
platform. `build.verbose` exists since 0.10, so the rename keeps working
with the 0.12.x releases upstream last built with.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [affects every platform's fresh build with scikit-build-core >= 1.0; upstream main still carries cmake.verbose]
---
 pyproject.toml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 765f9f8..9915dac 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ wheel.packages = ["src/clangd"]
 wheel.py-api = "py2.py3"
 cmake.version = ">=3.16.0"
 ninja.version = ">=1.10.0"
-cmake.verbose = true
+build.verbose = true
 logging.level = "DEBUG"
 
 [tool.pytest.ini_options]
-- 
2.43.0

